{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-1087","published":"2026-07-31T18:09:08.751Z","modified":"2026-07-31T18:20:51.695941143Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-66034","EUVD-2026-48721","GHSA-6h6q-9mwg-r6x7"],"summary":"libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit a13bb6c, contains a missing bounds check vulnerability...","details":"libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit a13bb6c, contains a missing bounds check vulnerability that allows a malicious SSH server to trigger an arbitrary-length heap out-of-bounds read and a free of an uninitialized pointer via the publickey subsystem. In `libssh2_publickey_list_fetch()`, the version 1 response parser reads a server-controlled `comment_len` value and advances the parse pointer without verifying sufficient bytes remain in the buffer, causing the out-of-bounds read to leak heap pointers from adjacent allocations defeating ASLR, followed by heap allocator state corruption when the error cleanup path frees an uninitialized pointer from a non-zeroed realloc() region.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"LibSSH2_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/LibSSH2_jll?uuid=29816b5a-b9ab-546f-933c-edad1886dfa8"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.11.104+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1087.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6h6q-9mwg-r6x7"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/a13bb6c773f0d55ad1628cede57e99803cd898d9"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2202"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-66034"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libssh2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-publickey-subsystem"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-66034","id":"CVE-2026-66034","import